stages.template:
You are a senior ontology analyst specializing in the video game domain.
Extract a concise and precise Semantic Requirements Document (SRD) for constructing a general-purpose, document-grounded video game ontology. Use background knowledge to understand terminology, normalize concepts, and identify reusable abstractions, but DO NOT introduce factual knowledge that is not supported by the source text.
Prefer terminology used in the document. Normalize obvious terminology variants only when needed for consistency.

=======================================


SRD JSON SCHEMA (keep entries tight; no fixed maximum):
{
  "key_concepts": [
    {"term": str, "type": "Entity|Role|Activity|Event|Category|Component|Attribute|TimeInstant|TimeInterval|Quantity|Claim", "definition": str}
  ],
  "relationships": [
        {"subject": str, "predicate": str, "object": str, "qualifiers": {"when?": str|null, "scope?": str|null}}
  ],
  "event_activities": [
        {"name": str, 
        "participants": [{"entity": str, "role": str}],
        "objects": [str],
        "context": str|null}
    ],
  "temporal_information": [
        {"name": str, "kind": "Instant|Interval|Duration|HistoricalPeriod", "value": str, "applies_to": str}
    ],
  "classifications": [
        {"parent": str, "child": str, "basis?": str|null}
    ],
  "claims": [
        {"about": str, "claim": str, "attributed_to": str|null, "key_criteria": [str]}
    ],
  "cq_alignment": [
        {"cq": str, "supported_by": ["key_concepts|relationships|event_activities|temporal_information|classifications|claims"], "notes?": str|null}
    ],
  "assumptions": [str]
}

INSTRUCTIONS:
• Prefer terminology used in the document and normalize obvious variants when useful.
• Extract the reusable concepts and relations needed to cover the CQs; do not enforce a fixed maximum number of concepts or relationships.
• Use Category for reusable types and Entity for specific named entities. Represent instance membership through relationships when needed rather than placing named entities in classifications.
• Use event_activities and claims only when genuinely necessary; leave them sparse rather than forcing every fact into these structures.
• Use classifications only for genuine taxonomic subtype relations. Do not use subclass relations merely to represent version, mode, platform, role, or contextual grouping when a relationship would be more appropriate.
• Ensure every CQ maps to cq_alignment. Use notes mainly for ambiguity or unsupported CQs; do not repeat the expected answer unnecessarily.
• Only include information present or reasonably implied by THIS text. If unknown, omit.
• Output JSON only.

### page_text ###
{page_text}

### cqs_for_page ###
{cqs_for_page}

Review the current Turtle syntax. This is text-only review; do not claim to have run RDFLib or any external validator.

### ontology_snapshot ###
{ontology_snapshot}

Review the current ontology for possible OWL inconsistencies. No OWL reasoner is available in this workflow; never report a verified consistency pass.

### ontology_snapshot ###
{ontology_snapshot}

Apply only fixes supported by the supplied feedback to the current ontology. If feedback is missing, do not invent a QA result or claim a completed repair. Return the complete ontology as valid Turtle.

### feedback ###
{feedback}

### ontology_snapshot ###
{ontology_snapshot}
